and adding to net_device_ops: .ndo_change_mtu = fbnic_change_mtu,
Reason:
The new change_mtu function checks, using fbnic_check_split_frames, whether the requested MTU would cause multi-fragment packets when the XDP program is attached. If so, it returns an error, preventing the MTU increase. This ensures that XDP programs expecting single-buffer packets continue to work correctly.

